Findings below.

## 1. The git client — `internal/git/client.go`

**How the exec.Cmd is constructed.** `internal/git/client.go` never touches `os/exec`. Every invocation goes through the `command.Runner` interface:

```go
// Client is a typed wrapper over the git binary rooted at a working directory.
type Client struct {
	Runner command.Runner
	Dir    string
}

func (g Client) run(ctx context.Context, args ...string) (string, error) {
	stdout, _, err := g.Runner.Run(ctx, g.Dir, "git", args...)
	return strings.TrimSpace(string(stdout)), err
}
```

The real process is built in `/Users/robinhultman/dev/intropy/tooling/intropy-cli/internal/command/runner.go`:

```go
func (ExecRunner) Run(ctx context.Context, dir, name string, args ...string) ([]byte, []byte, error) {
	cmd := exec.CommandContext(ctx, name, args...)
	cmd.Dir = dir

	var stdout, stderr bytes.Buffer
	cmd.Stdout = &stdout
	cmd.Stderr = &stderr

	err := cmd.Run()
	...
}
```

**Env handling: there is none.** `cmd.Env` is never assigned anywhere in the repo (grep for `cmd.Env`, `os.Environ`, `GIT_` returns zero hits outside test `t.Setenv` for `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`/`INTROPY_GITOPS_REPO`). So git inherits the full parent environment — no `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0`, no `GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM`, no `GIT_SSH_COMMAND`, no `-c` config overrides, no `LC_ALL`/`GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL` pinning. `cmd.Stdin` is also left nil. Error classification in `ExecRunner.Run`: context cancellation wins first, then `exec.ErrNotFound` → `*command.NotInstalledError`, then `*exec.ExitError` → `*command.ExitError{Name, Args, Dir, Code, Stderr}`.

**Exported surface of package `git`** (all methods on value receiver `Client`, none on pointer):

| Signature | git args actually run |
|---|---|
| `HEAD(ctx) (string, error)` | `rev-parse HEAD` |
| `Status(ctx, paths ...string) ([]string, error)` | `status --porcelain --untracked-files=all` [`--` paths…] |
| `Fetch(ctx, remote string, refspecs ...string) error` | `fetch --quiet <remote> refspecs…` |
| `DefaultBranch(ctx, remote string) (string, error)` | `symbolic-ref --short refs/remotes/<remote>/HEAD`, falling back to `ls-remote --symref <remote> HEAD` |
| `IsAncestor(ctx, ancestor, descendant string) (bool, error)` | `merge-base --is-ancestor a d`; exit 1 → `false, nil`, anything else → error |
| `Add(ctx, paths ...string) error` | `add -- paths…` |
| `CheckoutPaths(ctx, paths ...string) error` | `checkout -- paths…`; errors if `len(paths)==0` |
| `CreateBranch(ctx, name, startPoint string) error` | `checkout -B <name> <startPoint>` |
| `Switch(ctx, ref string) error` | `checkout <ref>` |
| `ResetHard(ctx, ref string) error` | `reset --hard <ref>` |
| `Clean(ctx) error` | `clean -fdq` |
| `RevParse(ctx, rev string) (string, error)` | `rev-parse <rev>` |
| `Commit(ctx, messages ...string) error` | `commit --quiet` + one `-m` per message; errors if no messages; no `-a` |
| `Tag(ctx, name, message, commit string) error` | `tag --annotate --message <msg> <name> <commit>` |
| `TagCommit(ctx, name string) (string, bool, error)` | `rev-parse --verify --quiet refs/tags/<name>^{commit}`; exit 1 → `"", false, nil` |
| `LastCommit(ctx, rev, path string) (string, bool, error)` | delegates to `LastCommitAt` |
| `LastCommitAt(ctx, rev, path string) (string, time.Time, bool, error)` | `log -1 --format=%H%x00%cI <rev> -- <path>`, parsed as RFC3339 |
| `Log(ctx, revRange string, paths ...string) ([]LogCommit, error)` | `log --format=%H%x00%s --no-merges <revRange>` [`--` paths…] |
| `Push(ctx, remote, refspec string) error` | `push --quiet <remote> <refspec>` |
| `Rebase(ctx, upstream string) error` | `rebase <upstream>` |
| `RebaseAbort(ctx) error` | `rebase --abort` |
| `Trailers(ctx, rev string) ([]Trailer, error)` | `log -1 --format=%(trailers:only=true) <rev>` |

Package-level: `func Clone(ctx context.Context, r command.Runner, url, dir string) error` → `r.Run(ctx, "", "git", "clone", "--quiet", url, dir)` (note: empty `dir` for cwd, so the clone happens in the process's cwd with an absolute/relative target path), and `func ShortSHA(rev string) string` (truncates to 7 only when `len(rev) >= 40`).

Exported types: `LogCommit{SHA, Subject}`, `Trailer{Key, Value}` with `String() string`, `PushRejectedError{Remote, Refspec, Stderr}`, `RebaseConflictError{Upstream, Stderr}`.

Rejection detection is stderr-substring based:

```go
func isRejection(stderr string) bool {
	for _, marker := range []string{"[rejected]", "non-fast-forward", "fetch first", "Updates were rejected"} {
		if strings.Contains(stderr, marker) {
			return true
		}
	}
	return false
}
```

Note `Rebase` treats *any* `*command.ExitError` as `*RebaseConflictError` (no stderr inspection).

## 2. gitops repository cache — `internal/gitops/repository.go`

**Cache dir derivation — the URL is hashed, opaquely:**

```go
// CheckoutDir derives a stable cache path from the remote URL. The URL is
// hashed rather than sanitised because the same repository can be named several
// ways (SSH, HTTPS, with or without .git) and because URLs contain characters
// that are awkward in paths.
func CheckoutDir(cacheRoot, url string) string {
	sum := sha256.Sum256([]byte(url))
	return filepath.Join(cacheRoot, hex.EncodeToString(sum[:])[:16])
}
```

The hash is over the **raw URL string with no normalization** — `git@host:acme/gitops.git` and `https://host/acme/gitops.git` and a trailing-`.git`-less variant each get a distinct 16-hex-char directory. Default root: `filepath.Join(os.UserCacheDir(), "intropy", "gitops")` via `defaultCacheRoot()`.

**Open path** (`Open(ctx, Options{URL, Runner, CacheRoot})`): require non-empty URL → default `Runner` to `command.ExecRunner{}` → resolve `cacheRoot` → `dir := CheckoutDir(cacheRoot, url)` → `os.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(dir), 0o755)` → `acquireLock(dir + ".lock")` (`os.OpenFile` + `syscall.Flock(LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB)`, `EWOULDBLOCK` → "another intropy deploy is already using the cached GitOps checkout") → construct `&Repository{Root: dir, URL: url, lock: lock}` with `Git: git.Client{Runner: r, Dir: dir}` → `refresh` (on error: `Close()` then return).

**Refresh/clone:**

```go
func (w *Repository) refresh(ctx context.Context, r command.Runner) error {
	if _, err := os.Stat(filepath.Join(w.Root, ".git")); err != nil {
		if !errors.Is(err, fs.ErrNotExist) {
			return fmt.Errorf("inspect %s: %w", w.Root, err)
		}
		// A directory without .git is the debris of an interrupted clone;
		// git clone refuses to write into it, so clear it first.
		if err := os.RemoveAll(w.Root); err != nil {
			return fmt.Errorf("clear %s: %w", w.Root, err)
		}
		if err := git.Clone(ctx, r, w.URL, w.Root); err != nil {
			return err
		}
	}

	branch, err := w.Git.DefaultBranch(ctx, RemoteName)
	if err != nil {
		return err
	}
	w.Branch = branch

	if err := w.Git.Fetch(ctx, RemoteName, branch); err != nil {
		return err
	}
	// Hard reset, not pull ...
	if err := w.Git.ResetHard(ctx, RemoteName+"/"+branch); err != nil {
		return err
	}
	return w.Git.Clean(ctx)
}
```

**Origin handling: `remote.origin.url` is never read and never set.** The only origin concept is the constant `const RemoteName = "origin"` (used as a *name* argument in `DefaultBranch`/`Fetch`/`ResetHard`/`Push` here and in `internal/deploy/publish.go`, `wait.go`, `init.go`, `internal/source/source.go`). Grep across all `.go` files for `remote.origin`, `get-url`, `remote add`, `config --get`: the only hits are three test lines (`internal/deploy/publish_test.go:194` `remote set-url`, `internal/git/client_test.go:219` `remote set-head`, `:372` `remote add`). Consequence: an existing cached checkout is **reused whenever the hash matches**, and the checkout's actual configured origin is never validated against `Options.URL`. Conversely, the same repo addressed by a differently-spelled URL silently re-clones into a second cache dir. `Repository.URL` is only consumed by `git.Clone` inside `refresh`.

Other exported bits: `Repository{Root, URL, Branch string; Git git.Client; lock *os.File}`, `Close()` (unlock + close, nil-safe/idempotent, keeps the checkout), `Options{URL, Runner, CacheRoot}`, `CachedRoot(gitopsRepoOverride string) (string, error)` — loads config, `RequireGitopsRepo()`, `defaultCacheRoot()`, `CheckoutDir`, then stats `<dir>/.git`; never clones or fetches (backs shell completion).

## 3. Test infrastructure

**Real `git` is used everywhere — there is no fake git binary and no fake git script on PATH.** `/Users/robinhultman/dev/intropy/tooling/intropy-cli/internal/gittest/gittest.go` states it outright: "Real git rather than a fake: clone, fetch, reset and ancestry are exactly the operations where a mock encodes our assumptions instead of git's behaviour. The git binary is available wherever this repository's tests run." The only `.sh` file in the repo is `./install.sh`; there is no `testdata` directory anywhere.

Helper functions:

- `/Users/robinhultman/dev/intropy/tooling/intropy-cli/internal/gittest/gittest.go` — `NewRepo(t, branch) string` (temp dir, one commit of `README.md` containing `"hello\n"`); `Init(t, dir, branch)` which runs `init --quiet --initial-branch=`, `config user.email test@example.com`, `config user.name Test`, `config commit.gpgsign false`, `config receive.denyCurrentBranch ignore` (so a non-bare dir can serve as origin); `Run(t, dir, args...) string` (bare `exec.Command("git", args...)` with `cmd.Dir = dir`, `CombinedOutput`, no env manipulation); `Commit(t, dir, path, content, message)`; `WriteFile(t, path, content)`; `ReadFile(t, path) string`; `HEAD(t, dir) string`.
- `/Users/robinhultman/dev/intropy/tooling/intropy-cli/internal/gitops/gitopstest/gitopstest.go` — `DeployYAML`, `BaseDeployment` consts, `ComponentYAML(name, image, envs)`, type `Component{Coordinate, Image, Environments, OverlayImages}`, `NewRepo(t, components ...Component) string`. Deliberately does not import `gitops` (cycle avoidance + literal layout).
- `/Users/robinhultman/dev/intropy/tooling/intropy-cli/internal/git/client_test.go` — `testClient(dir) Client` returning `Client{Runner: command.ExecRunner{}, Dir: dir}`, and `type failingRunner struct{}` whose `Run` always returns `errors.New("boom")` (the only stub Runner in the git tests, used solely to check error wrapping). Tests that need a push target clone with `git.Clone` and then re-`config` user.email/user.name/commit.gpgsign in the clone (the clone does not inherit the origin's local config).
- `/Users/robinhultman/dev/intropy/tooling/intropy-cli/internal/gitops/repository_test.go` — `openOpts(t, url) Options` returning `Options{URL: url, Runner: command.ExecRunner{}, CacheRoot: t.TempDir()}`. Important comment on why the cache is injected rather than HOME-redirected: on macOS a mismatched HOME makes every git call stall ~5s, turning the file into a 90-second run. Tests: clone-then-reuse, picks up new commits, discards debris, recovers from interrupted clone, exclusivity (`strings.Contains(err.Error(), "already using")`), requires URL, `TestCheckoutDirIsStablePerURL` (asserts SSH vs HTTPS map to *different* dirs and that the basename has no `@:/`), Close idempotent.
- Other gitops test helpers: `newGitopsRepo(t, map[string][]string) string` and `componentYAML(name, envs)` in `internal/gitops/layout_test.go`; `writeDeployYAML(t, root, content)` in `config_test.go`; `writeComponentYAML(t, content) string` in `kind_test.go`. `platform_test.go` has no helpers.
- Downstream fixtures reusing this infra: `newRepoFixture(t)`/`planFixture`/`requireKustomize` (skips when kustomize absent) in `internal/deploy/plan_test.go`, `newSourceClone(t) (clone, origin string)` and `newRunFixture`/`newRunFixtureWithImage` in `internal/deploy/service_test.go` (which set `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` and blank `INTROPY_GITOPS_REPO`, then write `gitopsRepo: <origin>`), plus `f.cacheRoot` + `gitops.CheckoutDir(f.cacheRoot, f.gitopsOrigin)` used in `service_test.go:158/295/435`, `diff_test.go:440`, `init_test.go:303`. `internal/command/runner_test.go` has `type fakeRunner` with `Run` and `called(substr)`.

## 4. Existing URL normalization / parsing helpers

**There is no git-URL normalization or comparison helper anywhere in the repo.** Confirmed by grepping all `.go` files for `normaliz`, `url.Parse`, `TrimSuffix(...git`, `ssh://`, `scp`, `get-url`. What exists is unrelated:

- `/Users/robinhultman/dev/intropy/tooling/intropy-cli/internal/kustomize/manifest.go` — `Normalize([]byte)`, `NormalizeJSON([]string)`, `Identities()`: YAML manifest canonicalisation, nothing to do with URLs.
- `/Users/robinhultman/dev/intropy/tooling/intropy-cli/internal/argocd/client.go:74` — `url.Parse(server)` for the ArgoCD API base (`&url.URL{Scheme: scheme, Host: server}`), an HTTP endpoint, not a git remote.
- `/Users/robinhultman/dev/intropy/tooling/intropy-cli/internal/deploy/init.go:396-399` — `normalizeSystemName(s string)` folds spellings of a *system name* (closest existing pattern for a small unexported normalizer + its lookup at lines 382-389).
- `/Users/robinhultman/dev/intropy/tooling/intropy-cli/internal/config/config.go` — `GitopsRepo` is carried as an opaque string: field `GitopsRepo string \`yaml:"gitopsRepo"\`` (line 49), resolution `GitopsRepo: cmp.Or(flags.GitopsRepo, os.Getenv(EnvGitopsRepo), c.GitopsRepo)` (line 131), and `RequireGitopsRepo()` (line 138) which only checks non-empty. No syntax validation, no scheme handling, no `.git` trimming.

So if you need to compare two git URLs (ssh vs https, trailing `.git`, `git@host:path` scp-form vs `ssh://git@host/path`), nothing exists to build on — and note the deliberate design comment in `CheckoutDir` plus `TestCheckoutDirIsStablePerURL` asserting `a != b` for the SSH/HTTPS pair, which pins the current "no normalization" behaviour into the test suite.

